Z||000003||ricksmastermix||11-23-2001||03:11 PM||||If you are looking for a great subwoofer for your fiero, do what I did. I converted the original Fiero enclosure to a dual 6.5" Iso-barik configuration. You'll need a 6" PVC coupler from any building supply store, two 6.5" Polyprop. speakers from Radio Shack, 19.95 ea.,a tube of silcone rubber, heavy guage speaker wire and a small piece of 1/2" plywood. Total cost under $60.<BR>This type of design was only licensed to one audio manufacturer in the U.S. for years and not widely used. But, it performs incredibly well. Contact me if you're interested.<BR>Rick||||reg||1
